<<~ aka "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/RFC-2119#/normative-language">>

<<^ code="&#x0002;">>

<<~ ahu #/head>>

! Cap-Tier ~ the sealing posture the quine declares and the gate tightens

> Status: PROPOSED — operator-ruled (2026-07-21), the CORE built (`66594fae` `cap-tier.ts`; `30cdd087`
> authenticated keyring delivery). The floor stands wired live; the declared-source rides a defined-but-
> unlit shore. The //model// awaits a post-swarm hoike.

A bag answers ''one question'' about its sealing — WHO holds the read-cap — and the answer rides as a ''chain by set-inclusion'': VEIL{this-vessel} ⊂ PERSONAGROUP{your-fleet} ⊂ CONTRACT{your-fleet ∪ a-cabal} ⊂ PUBLIC{world}. The bag ''declares'' its tier as self-describing data; the gate ''enforces'' the meet of that declaration against the crypto floor — so a declaration ''only ever tightens'', mechanically never loosens. The whole model turns on that one asymmetry.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/posture>>

!! The posture ~ sealed everywhere, cleartext only at the human surfaces

''Operator ruling (2026-07-21): no cleartext in the write at all — cleartext lives ONLY at the two human surfaces.'' Everything that leaves a vessel travels ''ciphertext''; plaintext survives in exactly two places, and both are where a ''person'' reads or edits — the browser DOM and the local-filesystem projection (#content-resolution names the disk projection). VEIL names the cleartext-local floor (nothing crosses a vessel boundary in the clear); PUBLIC names the world-readable shelf; the two member tiers travel sealed on the wire and open only for their recipient set. Sealing-on-the-wire stays ''universal'' — the tier never decides //whether// to seal, only //who holds the read-cap//.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-chain>>

!! The chain ~ four read-cap holder-sets, one total order

The tier names the read-cap holder-set, ascending in openness — a lower rank names a ''smaller'' set (fewer readers → more restrictive):

<<~ scale captier "veil@0 ~ {this-vessel} · cleartext-local, nothing crosses in the clear -> personagroup@1 ~ {your-fleet} · keyring-delivered to the operator's own persona fleet -> contract@2 ~ {your-fleet ∪ a-cabal} · keyring-delivered to the fleet PLUS a contracted cabal -> public@3 ~ {world} · the deterministically-federatable public shelf">>

''TWO RATCHETS, OPPOSITE DIRECTIONS, ORTHOGONAL PLANES.'' This chain ratchets ''tighter'' — a declaration only ever narrows the read-cap holder-set, mechanically never widens it. The dwelling plane ratchets the other way: `nohopapa` ''deposits'' depth by staying, and erodes when tending stops (`identity-enacts-relation`). Disclosure narrows; dwelling deepens. `papa` carries //layer · rank · structured sequence// and BOTH planes read as strata — which is exactly why they must stay named apart. ''A deep dweller holds no wider read-cap, and a public bag confers no depth.'' Fusing them would let standing buy disclosure, which is the shape this stack refuses.

''PERSONAGROUP and CONTRACT ride the SAME mechanism'' — keyring-delivery to a recipient set (#/keyring-delivery) — differing ONLY in which set (`fleet ⊂ fleet∪cabal`, a strict chain). A Cabal STARTS a cross-operator contract (#carry-contract names the bilateral tier the cabal negotiates); PERSONAGROUP reads as a SELF-contract to your own device-admitted vessels. The four names carry the human face; the specific recipient set rides beneath.

''THE ONE PLANE THAT TRUNCATES THE CHAIN.'' A ''reach credential'' — a foreign app credential the vessel holds so a human posts outward from their wiki (#/reach-plane) — rides this same chain and this same keyring-delivery, and stops one rung short: ''PUBLIC is refused by TYPE'', because a world-readable credential stops being a credential. So the reach ceiling reads CONTRACT where the content chain carries none, and the difference names a definition rather than a policy. A credential declared PERSONAGROUP delivers to the whole fleet — every device of yours may post — and a credential ''never federates'' in any tier. On that plane ''the tier IS the blast radius'', so the tighten-only keystone below reads as a security control rather than hygiene.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/self-describing-datum>>

!! The self-describing datum ~ the quine speaks its own walls

The tier rides as a ''declared datum'' the @daemon recipe carries (a bag-level default; a per-tiddler `capTier` refines it). ''Fail-closed by construction'': `DEFAULT_CAP_TIER = "veil"`, and `parseCapTier` folds any torn / absent / unknown value to VEIL — a torn datum NEVER silently opens a bag.

Modeled ''isomorphic to `FederationPosture`'' (federation-gate.ts) by composition, never by an interface tower: a closed string union + a `DEFAULT_…` fail-closed constant + a `…FromDoc` parser that fail-closes a torn value + a pure gate fn. The tier carries ''one structure more'' than a posture — a total order + a `meet` (a posture reads as the two-valued special case). The rhyme is a subtraction, not an inheritance.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-keystone>>

!! The keystone ~ declare ⊥ enforce, so the quine can only self-tighten

''The load-bearing invariant.'' The datum only DECLARES; the gate ENFORCES `declared ∧ structural-floor` — the ''taint-meet'' toward the more-restrictive tier. A self-describing datum can therefore only ever ''self-TIGHTEN'': `resolveTier(declared, floor) = meet(declared, floor)` never returns a tier more-open than its floor, so it is ''mechanically impossible'' for a quine to grant more openness than the crypto structure permits. The gate never trusts the declared datum to loosen.

Three consequences fall out of the one meet:

* ''The high-water-mark cascade'' — `refineBagTierWithTiddlers` folds the bag default under `meet` with every per-tiddler refinement: a bag reads only as shareable as its ''least-shareable tiddler''. A tiddler declaring PUBLIC inside a PERSONAGROUP bag leaves the bag PERSONAGROUP.
* ''META-CAP ≥ declared cap'' — `mayDeclareTier`: the write-cap that SETS a bag's tier datum must sit at-least-as-restrictive as the tier it declares. You cannot publicly-editably declare a private bag's tier (attenuation-only, the ocap discipline of #orichalcum-capabilities).
* ''The gate adds a deny, never an allow'' — `capTierShareDecision` wraps `memberCarryShareDecision` verbatim; the structural base-deny stands ABSOLUTE (a tier never resurrects a doc the structure denied), and the tier predicate ANDs only over the base's `true`. With no declared datum it degenerates EXACTLY to the base — an inert shore.

The keystone reads back through the code: revert the meet to take the more-OPEN and nine tests fall, the gate withdrawal among them.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/declassification>>

!! Declassification ~ the one-way ratchet under no-global-now

Tightening is free — a bag may always self-tighten, and a tightening cascade never asks the operator. ''Loosening'' (moving toward more openness) is a different act: `mayDeclassify` grants it ONLY under the operator-root capability — never content-derived (''robust declassification''), so no datum an adversary can influence can widen a bag. And the ratchet runs ''one way under no-global-now'' (#/causal-islands): a declassification widens who reads ''new'' writes, but it cannot un-federate the ''past'' — bytes already carried to a holder-set stay carried, because a causal island cannot reach back across another's log. A re-tightening never recalls what already crossed.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/keyring-delivery>>

!! Keyring delivery ~ the member read-cap, delivered AUTHENTICATED

The member tiers (PERSONAGROUP / CONTRACT) become concrete through ''keyring-delivery to the recipient set'' (built `30cdd087`). The per-Nexus convergence keyring — the `@cad` read-key (#/content-resolution) — rides ''admission'': the founder seals its `{epoch → secret}` keyring to the joinee's ephemeral X25519 recipient on the persona-admit grant hop (#/persona-policy), and the joinee installs it ''authoritatively'' — a delivered epoch supersedes the joinee's self-minted PHANTOM (a first-boot Nexus-of-one that seals only bodies no peer can read). Same-Nexus members thereby share the secret → cross-member `@cad` read works.

''The lesson, load-bearing: a delivery must be as AUTHENTICATED as the ceremony it rides.'' The recipient pubkey rode PUBLIC in the enrollment offer, so a ''sealed-only'' fragment proves nothing about WHO authored it — an active paster could substitute their own keyring, sealed to that same public key, and the joinee would seal every future body under an attacker-known secret. Confidential ≠ authenticated when the recipient key is public. The cure ''binds a sha256 of the exact carried token INTO the persona-signed grant transcript''; the joinee installs ONLY on a signature-covered digest match, else stays carry-only (four fail-closed branches). Revert the digest gate and the MITM-substitution test falls — the binding genuinely catches the swap.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/groundings>>

!! Groundings ~ the falsifiable rhymes

The model reads as a real pattern integrity because independent fields under their own selection pressure each landed on a piece. The discipline: ''weight the falsifiable engineering/security rhymes; treat metaphysics as vocabulary, never evidence.''

| Rhyme | Grounds | Field |
|---|---|---|
| ''Denning lattice model'' of secure information flow; Bell-LaPadula "no read up" | the four tiers form a ''chain lattice''; `meetCapTier` IS the lattice meet toward the more-restrictive (a total order → a bounded meet-semilattice) | information-flow security |
| ''High-water-mark'' floating-label taint | `refineBagTierWithTiddlers` = the confidentiality high-water: a container tightens to the most-restrictive of its contents | dynamic taint / IFC |
| ''Robust declassification'' (Myers · Sabelfeld · Sands) | `mayDeclassify` = loosening is a privileged operator-root act an attacker cannot influence — the operator NAMED this pattern | language-based security |
| ''Anonymous sealed-box'' (`crypto_box_seal`) = sender-unauthenticated by construction; ''Signal X3DH signed prekey'' catches a substituted prekey by signature | the keyring lesson exactly — seal-to-public is confidential-not-authenticated → MITM; the fix binds the digest into the SIGNED transcript | applied cryptography |
| ''Object-capability'' deny-by-default + attenuation-only | `DEFAULT_CAP_TIER = veil` fail-closed; META-CAP ≥ declared = no amplification | ocap (#/orichalcum-capabilities) |
| ''MLS / TreeKEM'' group key delivery | keyring-delivery to a recipient set — ''PARTIAL: delivery, NOT agreement''; the mesh delivers a per-Nexus secret, it does not run a CGKA here | cryptography |

''The honest guard (Stranger's frame-check):'' the security lattice illuminates the ''order'' (the tiers), the ''meet'' (tighten-only), and the ''declassification'' (privileged, robust) — but it lies about the mechanism where it assumes a global reference monitor. Our gate is ''causal-island-local'' (#/causal-islands): it reads WHAT THIS NODE verifies as-of-last-sync, never a global census. Borrow the lattice-meet, the high-water-mark, and the robust-declassification act; never borrow the //global-now// a classical reference monitor assumes.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/provenance>>

!! Provenance ~ PROPOSED, the core built

This meme stands ''PROPOSED'' (crucible-before-binding). The CORE is built: `66594fae` (`mesh/cap-tier.ts` — the 4-tier total order + the keystone + the high-water-mark cascade + `mayDeclareTier`/`mayDeclassify`), `30cdd087` (the authenticated keyring delivery). ''Honest bounds, kept lit'':

* The ''structural FLOOR'' is wired live — `structuralFloorFor` reads the SAME federatable-set + sealed-plane oracles the carry-split already consults (a federatable plane floors at PUBLIC, a provably-sealed plane at CONTRACT, else VEIL).
* The ''declared SOURCE'' rides a defined-but-UNLIT shore — no @daemon recipe carries a `capTier` datum in the tree yet, so a live `declaredTierForDoc` returns null for every doc → the floor governs → zero behavior change. Lighting it needs the recipe-write path + a doc→bag resolver.
* ''PERSONAGROUP and CONTRACT collapse to "member peer" at the wire'' — the wire shore cannot itself split fleet from cabal, so CONTRACT reads as the honest structural ceiling of the sealed lane and a PERSONAGROUP refinement rides atop as a declared tightening.

Deferred with clean shores (not built): the TW5 `$:/tags/CapTierFilter` ordered-cascade rendering, the remote-vessel-edits-the-@daemon-recipe UX, the CLI/browser surfaces.

<<~/ahu>>

